{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979960-2e-help-with-focusing-on-mysteries","id":979960,"title":"[2e] Help with focusing on Mysteries","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-01T17:43:21-07:00","id":979960,"title":"[2e] Help with focusing on Mysteries","content":"I could use a hand. I understand the primary thrust behind Mage 2e is that the PCs are meant to be seekers of occult knowledge, obsessed with ferreting out all the secrets of the Fallen World and becoming masters of the unknown. I also understand the concept behind Mysteries (which, at the end of the day, <i>is </i>a bit of a vague term you'll admit), to be basically a catch all for &quot;supernatural effect of unknown provenance or operation&quot;, and that the rules are designed such that the PCs are meant to be actively studying them and solving them. <br /> <br /> But, I have to admit, at the end of the day, I'm not entirely sure what that should look like. <br /> <br /> To take a practical example, the idea that founding a Legacy is about studying an underlying Mystery through action and contemplation. Now, my players are all new to nWoD and Mage, so they have no knowledge of any of the Legacies from 1e. To that end a couple of them are already thinking they'd rather found their own Legacies. One PC is a Free Council social activist who wants to base a Legacy around Imbuing items to give to Sleepers to help them detect and resist magic (which I adore because of how suicidal yet awesome that will be), but what <i>Mystery </i>is explored in doing that? Like, what thing would be out there that they can find and study that would be appropriate for this? What can they Scrutinize? So far all I've got is &quot;they go study the construction of imbued items&quot;, but what would that entail, how can I make it appropriate for the Legacy, and above all, how can I make it entertaining? <br /> <br /> In general, I'm also curious how often you actually find your players Scrutinizing and Revealing magic, mine almost never do or even think to do it (in fact Active Mage Sight tends to slip their minds), and I'm not sure how to get them to <i>start </i>doing it. I've had to go &quot;you know, you <i>could </i>do this&quot; far too often for my liking. Additionally, how do you account for Mysteries often being threatening (like really, why would you Scrutinize the the Seers casting Fraying spells at you instead of returning fire?), and how do you build them into the story without it just turning into a drip feed of exposition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12121-ainsoph","name":"AinSoph","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T18:15:58-07:00","id":979975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AinSoph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979960-2e-help-with-focusing-on-mysteries#post979960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One PC is a Free Council social activist who wants to base a Legacy around Imbuing items to give to Sleepers to help them detect and resist magic (which I adore because of how suicidal yet awesome that will be), but what <i>Mystery </i>is explored in doing that? Like, what thing would be out there that they can find and study that would be appropriate for this? What can they Scrutinize? So far all I've got is &quot;they go study the construction of imbued items&quot;, but what would that entail, how can I make it appropriate for the Legacy, and above all, how can I make it entertaining?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm in the same boat as you. I could use more advice about mysteries, specifically when relating to Arcana. A ghost or spirit Mystery seems easy, it's just an odd Death or Spirit occurrence. What is a Matter mystery?<br /> <br /> That said, with this example, throwing it out there, the items seem more like they would work as a 'sixth sense' accessory. One thing you might have them do is study mages, and specifically Peripheral Mage Sight. The idea being that, since mages can passively detect magic, if you could find out why, an item might be able to give a comparable ability to a Sleeper. From there it's just finding ways to distract people or drive them away from situations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In general, I'm also curious how often you actually find your players Scrutinizing and Revealing magic, mine almost never do or even think to do it (in fact Active Mage Sight tends to slip their minds), and I'm not sure how to get them to <i>start </i>doing it. I've had to go &quot;you know, you <i>could </i>do this&quot; far too often for my liking. Additionally, how do you account for Mysteries often being threatening (like really, why would you Scrutinize the the Seers casting Fraying spells at you instead of returning fire?), and how do you build them into the story without it just turning into a drip feed of exposition? </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure but I don't think you would spend time scrutinizing dangerous spells cast at you, though you might do something risky like get an antagonist to use an ability at you. Perhaps it would sort of be like Weyland-Yutani in their 'dealings' with the xenomorphs. It would be ideal to catch one alive, but if that can't happen you could at least throw other people at it and see what it does to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T18:28:30-07:00","id":979982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979960-2e-help-with-focusing-on-mysteries?p=979975#post979975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm in the same boat as you. I could use more advice about mysteries, specifically when relating to Arcana. A ghost or spirit Mystery seems easy, it's just an odd Death or Spirit occurrence. What is a Matter mystery?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seemingly impossible substances with strange, esoteric means of production. For example, a cheap brand of kitchen knives that when stabbed into living wood turns the surrounding material into extremely pure silver. Analyzing it reveals the property to not be the result of supernal magic but a property of the metal itself, which, while chemically identical to steel, is symbolically something completely different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T18:50:31-07:00","id":979992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979960-2e-help-with-focusing-on-mysteries?p=979982#post979982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seemingly impossible substances with strange, esoteric means of production. For example, a cheap brand of kitchen knives that when stabbed into living wood turns the surrounding material into extremely pure silver. Analyzing it reveals the property to not be the result of supernal magic but a property of the metal itself, which, while chemically identical to steel, is symbolically something completely different.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Okay, but how do you make a story out of that? And, how do you make the PCs actually need to use Focused Mage Sight to get answers? Like, in this case, I'm immediately wondering who are the listed manufacturers and where are they coming from, which my PCs would solve mundanely. They might study the knives to get some answers about who the manufacturer is for purposes of assessing a threat, but they're unlikely to care outside of that unless it's related to their Obsessions or Aspirations, or their backstories. The knives in themselves aren't a threat, so there's no conflict inherently emanating from them that depends upon understanding them, and thus it doesn't really drive narrative. Or perhaps I'm reading it incorrectly? Again, need a hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12121-ainsoph","name":"AinSoph","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T19:01:48-07:00","id":979997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AinSoph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979960-2e-help-with-focusing-on-mysteries?p=979992#post979992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Okay, but how do you make a story out of that? And, how do you make the PCs actually need to use Focused Mage Sight to get answers? Like, in this case, I'm immediately wondering who are the listed manufacturers and where are they coming from, which my PCs would solve mundanely. They might study the knives to get some answers about who the manufacturer is for purposes of assessing a threat, but they're unlikely to care outside of that unless it's related to their Obsessions or Aspirations, or their backstories. The knives in themselves aren't a threat, so there's no conflict inherently emanating from them that depends upon understanding them, and thus it doesn't really drive narrative. Or perhaps I'm reading it incorrectly? Again, need a hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was mostly answering the question of what a Matter Mystery could be, but lets see what I can cook up here.<br /> <br /> You'll need to figure out where the manufacturers are, go there, inspect their methods of production, and then determine what factors are actually contributing to the magical effect the knives possess. Yes, some of these things can be solved mundanely, but some things you're going to have to use magic and Mage Sight to figure out. Whether the makers are a threat or not is pretty much up to you but I was generally thinking that the people making the knives are just normal people making knives. Whatever it is that's giving the knives this property is completely unknown to them, they don't even know it's a thing. Which means something, be that something an aspect of where the knives are made, a specific set of circumstances around how they're made, or something else of the like. <br /> <br /> Also, it doesn't need to cause conflict. The simple need to <i>know</i> is all that a lot of mages would need. Now making your players care is kinda on the ST. Specifics are going to almost completely depend on the characters and what they care about/how interested they are in exploring the unknown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T19:54:25-07:00","id":980020,"title":"","content":"I think it should be pointed out that the game doesn't require that Mysteries be solved via Scrutiny. In the end Mage Sight won't reveal more than the proper Knowing or Unveiling spell will, what Scrutiny can do is provide hints on what kinds of spells might be best designed for figuring a Mystery out, and/or brute force its way to the heart of the Mystery. Something Scrutiny does that Knowing and Unveiling spells don't do is tell you, &quot;That's it, there's nothing else to find here.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T20:05:26-07:00","id":980026,"title":"","content":"I guess, yeah. So Mysteries themselves aren't really the things that are going to be getting players after them. But Mysteries tied to Obsessions and Aspirations have some incentive built in. And I think you get some special Beats for understanding a worthwhile encounter with the supernatural.<br /> <br /> So to go with Ashenrogue's example, it might not be something that really leads the players anywhere. But if it somehow tied into the Obsession of the characters, for instance their mentor was found killed, their body entirely converted to silver, finding the knife and locating the manufacturer and other people who have that knife might work towards the hows and whys.<br /> <br /> For what it's worth I think Signs of Sorcery is really going to expand on Mysteries, and <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxveHUKxwBU9YzBRVWpGYzNFZ0U/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">the Mage Sight expansion</a> really offers some clarifications of mechanics involved, as well as things that could detract from a character's ability to identify things through it, including the linking of smaller Mysteries into larger ones.<br /> <br /> It sounds as if Mysteries can really be anything, from a mage's lingering spell to the bits of a corpse left behind from a werewolf's hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-01-2016, 11:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T21:24:10-07:00","id":980061,"title":"","content":"Totally reasonable question in the OP. I've been running a chronicle for about 10 sessions and finished 2 stories, let me see what I can offer.<br /> <br /> My PCs are probably using Scrutiny/Revelation...every/every other session? It almost always happens when I prompt them &quot;this is something your Scrutiny could help with,&quot; or &quot;do you want to turn Active Sight on? What Arcana?&quot; I imagine it like an adventure game where I'm telling them &quot;your cursor turns blue when you highlight this object!&quot; It seems like my players are a little different than I am when I get to play Mage, I'm usually very curious and active whereas they tend to lean more &quot;enjoying it, but more along for the ride.&quot; When they do latch onto something as especially interesting I lean on that hard and make it more important.<br /> <br /> Just as an example because I was thinking about it too: my players investigated a Matter Mystery for a lot of the first story. In the first session, a situation arose where they wanted to buy some coke to use as Soft Leverage in Social Maneuvering. I had the dealer mention a new hallucinogenic drug, and offer them a free sample to get them interested- making sure to heavily imply that there was something unusual or supernatural about it. One of my PCs is an Obrimos scientist who used Zoom In to examine the pill's chemical structure, and found the High Speech glyph for Matter fractally repeating at the molecular level, which got them curious. So I'm going out of my way as ST to tell them &quot;THIS IS SUPERNATURAL, CHECK IT OUT.&quot;<br /> <br /> Eventually one of the PCs took the drug (because a demon of Vice used its Influence), and started having an incredible powerful hallucination. Another PC found this weird and, after subduing the Vice demon, I reminded him that he could Scrutinize her with Mind Sight to see what was happening. So we did, and he didn't get enough successes and decided not to roll further to avoid contaminating the Mystery. The first PC is still unconscious and drooling. So they decide to go visit their more powerful Mentor to get help. Somewhere in there was some Active Matter Sight that got some confusing results (the pills are Availability 6+, or as I put it, &quot;the most valuable substance in the Fallen World&quot;), so they did Scrutiny and found that it was made of Apeiron, the Lead of Stygia. Which just raises further questions.<br /> <br /> It was great! They were legitimately interested and wanted to find out what was going on, especially because there were concrete stakes: &quot;you need to figure out what's happening because one of the PCs is gonna die if you don't fix this.&quot; It helps that my players uh, don't really care that much about their stated Aspirations and Obsessions, so they're very willing to listen to my suggestions of stuff to do.<br /> <br /> Some other things my PCs have used Scrutiny on:<ul><li>They were in a labyrinth and found a section of wall that they could walk through and didn't know why/didn't want to die in a trap. Another Matter Mystery! (It had Ghostwall cast on it.)</li> <li>An important Sleepwalker NPC had a couple of spells cast on their Pattern (seen in Prime Sight), one PC was curious and wanted to know what they were.</li> <li>Their Sanctum has a haunting, and it's not a ghost. They tried Active Sight in a few different permutations and eventually found something in Time Sight- it's a Paradox effect that eludes easy explanation with a Knowing spell.</li> <li>Their Mentor was acting strangely during a conversation, someone's Peripheral Sight went off, a PC turned on Time Sight and saw temporal warping around her- they quickly used Revelation and found that she had used Shifting Sands to relive the current scene.</li> <li>Their Mentor's Sanctum has completely disappeared from Space, the lot is empty, and no one remembers her. Once they actually found what to look for with standard Knowing spells (Pierce Deception helped), they did Space Scrutiny and found that it was the target of a &quot;Quarantine&quot; spell, and discovered one of the Keys as Deep Information.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> I believe every single one of those was prompted by me saying &quot;do you want to Scrutinize this?&quot; My PCs have never turned on non-Ruling Arcana in Active Sight if I didn't bring up the possibility, and even then, sometimes they decide not to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AinSoph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979960-2e-help-with-focusing-on-mysteries#post979960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One PC is a Free Council social activist who wants to base a Legacy around Imbuing items to give to Sleepers to help them detect and resist magic (which I adore because of how suicidal yet awesome that will be), but what <i>Mystery </i>is explored in doing that? Like, what thing would be out there that they can find and study that would be appropriate for this? What can they Scrutinize? So far all I've got is &quot;they go study the construction of imbued items&quot;, but what would that entail, how can I make it appropriate for the Legacy, and above all, how can I make it entertaining?</div> </div> </div> </div>My suggestion would be to have them give a Sleeper an Imbued Item, and then have them (covertly? overtly?) study the effect it has on that particular Sleepers life over time. Get your PC invested in the completely nonmagical, but still uniquely interesting concerns of this person's life, and see whether they use magic to try to fix it. Have them study what happens when the Sleeper inevitably causes Dissonance by being around magic. Is their Pattern affected by being around an Imbued Item all the time? (Answer: yes, it is.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 10-02-2016, 12:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T22:13:02-07:00","id":980092,"title":"","content":"This thread on rpgNet discusses the same thing, with limited results, but you might find some of it useful: <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?784464-Mage-the-Awakening-2e-Let-s-talk-about-Mysteries\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php...bout-Mysteries</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T22:15:51-07:00","id":980095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979960-2e-help-with-focusing-on-mysteries?p=980061#post980061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe every single one of those was prompted by me saying &quot;do you want to Scrutinize this?&quot; My PCs have never turned on non-Ruling Arcana in Active Sight if I didn't bring up the possibility, and even then, sometimes they decide not to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very helpful post, for me at least. I hope you get to a point where they start doing it on their own, though that's more of a player thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T22:23:23-07:00","id":980102,"title":"","content":"I'm glad it was helpful! I always find play experience way more useful than abstract theorycrafting.<br /> <br /> I think it's a matter of comfort with the rules. I'm hopeful that if we play long enough, they'll be more proactive. I'm consciously making a point in the first few stories of introducing new elements of the setting and new rules to play with (Astral travel, Supernal summoning, Duel Arcane, etc), hoping that they start to think of them as part of their toolbox automatically. I really enjoy my players and they're enjoying and involved in our chronicle, it's just a matter of conveying &quot;this is something you can do&quot; and then creating situations where Mage Sight is a necessary solution. Look at the descriptions for what each Active Sight shows you and ask &quot;when would it be useful to know this?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T22:35:29-07:00","id":980105,"title":"","content":"Scrutiny mechanics are just fancy way to get info about new problem. It is handy, from time to time, but don't sweat when players are not using it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Mine players use <i>all the time</i> Active Mage Sight to check 'if there are weird things under X Arcanum' thing, as it is much quicker. It's not a heart of Mysteries seeking in game. I don't bother in writing proper <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/866755-mystery-sheet-for-2e\">Mystery Sheet</a> if the thing researched is not starting point of whole story, at least.<br /> <br /> The heart of Mysteries <b><i>is</i></b> <b><i>in characters Obsessions </i></b>- Arcane Beats as reward are more than enough for players to plunge in the Mysteries all around them. There is <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/974408-stories-of-obsession\">great topics on that very idea</a> - I just have simple advice to all on this: <b>Give one extra Obsession slot for all characters ( above normal Gnosis limit ) and commit it to cabal's / chronicle main Obsession</b>.<br /> <br /> In my London's 'You can be possible next Magic Jesus' game this slot is occupied on 'Are we Hieromagus?' Obsession and in Boston Alchemical play it's for simple 'Philosophers Stone' that is main Mystery of chronicle. If you get this common Obsession of characters, play is much more coherent and players like to cooperate on main story to generate Arcane Beats for themselves. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Then just tell from time to time your players 'You can get Arcane Beat from this Obsession by doing this' and they will be more than happy to sell their soul to the devil... eee, engage in story about those Mysteries. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-02-2016, 01:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T16:50:32-07:00","id":980473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979960-2e-help-with-focusing-on-mysteries?p=980061#post980061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Totally reasonable question in the OP. I've been running a chronicle for about 10 sessions and finished 2 stories, let me see what I can offer.</div> </div> </div> </div>This whole reply has been quite helpful. So the way I'm thinking of structuring it now is:<br /> <br /> -Peripheral Mage Sight = Something is up<br /> -Active Mage Sight = Is it something obvious/directly in my wheelhouse?<br /> -Scrutiny = This might be a problem, but I don't know enough to make a call and act<br /> <br /> Whereas the general concept of personal Mysteries is &quot;aspects of the supernatural my PCs pursue on their own time&quot;<br /> While more location/Consilium based Mysteries are &quot;things that let my villains have a grand plot or my Chronicle have a unique terrain&quot;<br /> And Story-based ones are &quot;shady stuff having an effect&quot;<br /> <br /> This structure lets me think about personal Mysteries as being where we bring in character development, Story as bringing in plots, and location as bringing in overarching narrative. That would make it easier to parse and distribute information, for sure. And it does save me from the fear that they need to be Scrutinizing the whole time or I'm doing it wrong. Granted, it does highlight how much system and lore knowledge you need before writing anything, but that's not new to Mage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The heart of Mysteries <b><i>is</i></b> <b><i>in characters Obsessions </i></b>- Arcane Beats as reward are more than enough for players to plunge in the Mysteries all around them. There is<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/974408-stories-of-obsession\">great topics on that very idea</a> - I just have simple advice to all on this: <b>Give one extra Obsession slot for all characters ( above normal Gnosis limit ) and commit it to cabal's / chronicle main Obsession</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem with this is I don't <i>have </i>a Main Chronicle Obsession. This was admittedly part of the reason I came here, because I wasn't sure if I needed magical dead zones with a long background causal explanation, or some such, to be running Mage properly, but I'm seeing more of their dramatic function here and how you don't really need one. I generally prefer the idea of the Storyteller responding to what the characters want to do than a mandate from on high, though I totally see how that can add coherency in your case. I don't think XP would actually incentivize my own players, y'see, they're decidedly non-powergamers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12121-ainsoph","name":"AinSoph","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T01:11:50-07:00","id":980644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AinSoph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979960-2e-help-with-focusing-on-mysteries?p=980473#post980473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think XP would actually incentivize my own players, y'see, they're decidedly non-powergamers.</div> </div> </div> </div>So they are a bit bad Mage players, as being Power-Obssesed-Character is main theme of the game - Mage players <i>should</i> be powergamers by game definition. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Really, just remember them that all those shiny new Artifacts, Status, Rotes and Attainments costs Arcane XP - I'm sure they will dwell more easily in to Obsessions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, not having main story Obsession maybe a too much Sandbox to make coherent game. You can run as you like it, but I strongly advise on <i>some</i> main Mystery to make play going by common threads. It maybe not main Mystery of the area even - my tow games are running on highly individual Mysteries of groups - secret of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/896878-2e-mystery-hieromagus-messiah-of-magic\">Hieromagus</a> and 7 'Atlantean Archmages' in one example, and looking for <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/668690-mystery-supernal-alchemy-philosopher-s-stone?p=876709#post876709\">Philosophers Stone</a> in second. Local High Mysteries of Concilium are a based of 'filler' subplots in proper game, but also nicely pointing to Obsessive nature of Awakened.<br /> <br /> Even Sandbox games should have main plot or your players do not have any idea to what choose in exploration order, in my experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T02:03:05-07:00","id":980664,"title":"","content":"You don't need a Chronicle Obsession, you could just as easily use a string of story obsessions as long as you can keep coming up with ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T02:41:11-07:00","id":980674,"title":"","content":"I'm basically borrowing what I see as the structure of DaveB's Soul Cage AP, where yes, there is a main narrative idea, but our monsters of the week provide immediate conflicts and worldbuilding, which in resolution provide clues and move the larger narrative gradually into focus. Classic A-plot and B-plot overlay. But that main narrative is mostly hidden, at least for the moment, and is at the &quot;what are the Seers up to?&quot; phase, which is not appropriate for an Obsession in my view. <br /> <br /> I do resent saying I have bad players though <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a>. Like, my aforementioned Libertine not *only* wants to smash the Veil, but the player happily took the True Friend merit at character gen for a Sleeper. He's already cast Stealing Fire on the guy despite knowing all about the Guardians, and explained all of Mage society to him. This they did in the third session. Last session they organised a full protest march to directly target a Seer corporation. It mighn't be occult powergaming, but it is Hubristic and awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12121-ainsoph","name":"AinSoph","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T02:53:26-07:00","id":980678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AinSoph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979960-2e-help-with-focusing-on-mysteries?p=980674#post980674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do resent saying I have bad players though <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a>. Like, my aforementioned Libertine not *only* wants to smash the Veil, but the player happily took the True Friend merit at character gen for a Sleeper. He's already cast Stealing Fire on the guy despite knowing all about the Guardians, and explained all of Mage society to him. This they did in the third session. Last session they organised a full protest march to directly target a Seer corporation. It mighn't be occult powergaming, but it is Hubristic and awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you <i>do</i> have Obsessions and Mysteries in play! Breaking the Veil ( i.e. Dissonance ) is as much appropriate Mystery as it can be. So your players ARE playing with Mysteries, only you do not see this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Just give them Arcane Beats for actions working with those supernatural phenomena and they will dwell in to their magical implication - i.e. Mysteries.<br /> <br /> I did not wanted to offend you or them here, only pointing that games is based on mechanical model that PCs are compelled by they own thirst for knowledge ( i.e. Arcane Beats ) to dwell in to shady things. Your players already doing that, only you do not reward them accordingly ( probably because you do not see this as magical conflict in first place ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T03:36:32-07:00","id":980691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979960-2e-help-with-focusing-on-mysteries?p=980678#post980678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did not wanted to offend you or them here, only pointing that games is based on mechanical model that PCs are compelled by they own thirst for knowledge ( i.e. Arcane Beats ) to dwell in to shady things. Your players already doing that, only you do not reward them accordingly ( probably because you do not see this as magical conflict in first place ).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah! I see what you mean now. See, I never thought of it that way because the character is not motivated to do things because they want to learn about it or because it'll offer them power or knowledge. They're doing it out of a sense of moral obligation informed by backstory as a Sleeper. It's not a Mystery to them, it's a Crusade. I do give Arcane beats for &quot;important/personal supernatural moment&quot; though, as opposed to &quot;exploring a Mystery. I supposed my lack of clarity regarding what Mysteries are/how they should work informed that =P.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12121-ainsoph","name":"AinSoph","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T04:10:35-07:00","id":980695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AinSoph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979960-2e-help-with-focusing-on-mysteries?p=980691#post980691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, I never thought of it that way because the character is not motivated to do things because they want to learn about it or because it'll offer them power or knowledge. They're doing it out of a sense of moral obligation informed by backstory as a Sleeper. It's not a Mystery to them, it's a Crusade.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have PCs Silver Ladder mentor that is Obrimos catholic priest. He 'just' want's to win the war on souls of Sleepers from Exarchs. But his actions lead him to have Obsessions 'Sleepers Dissonance' and 'Souls', as they are main points of his reaserches when he is doing his 'war on souls', he need to overcome those topics to really dwell in any possible way to win his future fight.<br /> <br /> Remember, in <b>Mage</b>, every time you look for something magical, it can be Mystery. If you want to do something supernatural - it will be Mystery. If you have mundane goals that need to overcome supernatural problem - it will be Mystery. Look also on Orders section of Mysteries they take - most often they are their 'mundane' actions, with usage of supernatural elements.<br /> <br /> Really, in play, characters mundane objectives become Obsessions quickly, as they sooner or later will go into supernatural area on pursuing those. Players want to fight with Exarchs? Great, now they need to overcome Dissonance in Sleeper compatriots, understand how Exarchs operate as Symbols-Tyrants or even how just Seers are communicating with their 'secret masters'. All of those will be nice, juicy Obsessions generating Arcane Beats.<br /> <br /> I also advise to leave them as much open as possible - better wording is 'Obsession: Exarchs' than 'Obsession: How Exarchs interacts with reality?' just because open-ended nature of first take make more possible ways for characters to generate Arcane Beats (i.e. making cool scenes/problems for themselves). Second take basically limits to 'we kidnap a Seer and make him spill the beans', where first one could lead even to things like Pentacle PCs trying to 'summon' Exarchs so they can say 'f@#k off!'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-03-2016, 07:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}